# g55-fu-cu-ssh -> DESKTOP-WIRE-G10

## s3-bridge-forward (bridge /command forwarding)

The core's bridge run (`computer_bridge_run.rs`) accepts the internal actions `owner_attach` and `owner_detach` because the desktop's
`/owner` endpoint sends them. The desktop's `/command` handler must refuse both with the same 400 `invalid request: invalid_action:
computer bridge action is not available` that Node's `assertPublicComputerRequest` gave (the bridge-server tests of the plan's
parity checklist), and `/owner` is the only place that sends them: a runtime must not attach an owner without holding a connection, nor
detach another runtime's owner.

## s2b renderer tests (no task owns them)

`settings/ssh-connect-dialog.test.mjs`, `settings/ssh-host-dialogs.test.mjs`, `remote-pc-switcher.test.mjs` (2 cases),
`connection-status-banner-*.test.mjs`, `composer-server-account.test.mjs` and `settings/connection-panel.test.mjs` (1 case) still mock
`window.mixdogDesktop.ssh*`; the components call `renderer/connections-core-api.ts`, whose client is `pcCoreClient()`. They need one
seam to run again: a test-only way to hand `core-direct/client.ts` a stub client (`openDirectClient` over a fake `CorePortBridge`, or a
setter marked test-only), then each `makeApi` answers `connections/ssh/*` requests instead of the preload methods.
